## CONTEXT BAND AND HANDOVER
At about 70% context start no new part. At about 75%, stop at a safe boundary: files whole, plants reverted (scratch copies discarded), every process you started stopped by pid, your port block free, your containers, networks and volumes removed, the lock released. Then write `/Volumes/Datasec_DEV/!CODING/Datasec/Datasec Security Composer/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-11_B1504_HANDOVER.md` (done / in hand / next / processes left / decisions a successor keeps: base sha, branch head, which parts are committed, the Q-answers as stamped, the base red set, the P-21 table so far), with last line `HANDOVER B1504: next <key> <step> | done <keys>`, and end STATUS with the same line.

## HARD STOP (slot)
At the HARD STOP clock: start nothing new. Push nothing unproven. If at least one part is committed with its checks green, push those commits only and end `PARTIAL B1504: <sha40> | done <parts> | not done <parts>`. Otherwise end `PARTIAL B1504: none | done <parts> | not done <parts>`, and write the HANDOVER.

## STANDING LINES
- **PRIOR-WORK CHECK** (Step 0b; a READY without a PRIOR WORK section is returned). Re-read main first; do not redo a ticket that is already fixed there: say which, with file and line.
- No message to any human. No comment or edit on any PR. **No Jira write** (this kit names none). Never delete (quarantine). **No deploy, no `az`, no hosted host or database, no image push.** The one outside read is Part 26a's anonymous registry read. No word added to any operator-facing text except the WORDS-27 slot's and the 21 record sentence the slot allows.
