- Red first for each behavioural change: a test that fails at base for the stated reason, then passes. `always-verify-and-check` and `no-skip-on-failure`: a red you cannot explain is a STOP; never skip a failing step.
- **Commit rules:** one commit per built part, subject in plain words. No ticket key, brief number, card id or person's name in any message. Check with `/usr/bin/grep -c -i -E 'B[0-9]{3,4}|PCOMP|Tuesday|Wednesday|Friday'` plus a name scan: count 0, and a planted control counts 1. **The name scan is underscore-aware:** for each name in the project's records (the product owner's first and family names and his deputy's, as `CLARIFICATIONS.md` names them; write them into your scratch scan file, never into a message), use `(?<![A-Za-z])<name>(?![a-z])` with `re.I`. Its control plants `_by_<name>_` and must fire. Run it over each message and every added line (the new scripts' comments included). Exactly ONE trailer: the attribution line your own session reminder gives (count 1). No `.env`, no secret; record gitleaks (`scripts/secret-scan.sh` as written, or the pre-commit hook) at each commit. ONE plain push of ONE ref, `HEAD:refs/heads/b1504/composer-lane-c-stack-deploy-hygiene` (never `--force`, never `+`). The ref must be absent before the push.
- **Git identity is never overridden.** Use the repo's own configured identity only, as the IDENTITY slot establishes it. Never `git -c user.name/user.email`, never `GIT_AUTHOR_*` / `GIT_COMMITTER_*`. Your READY section prints `git log --format='%h %ae | %ce'` for every new commit, each equal to that configured email.
